The index remains related to the payload because construction
checks the dependent second component and the join opens
one package, not two independently chosen values. If a
predecessor provides $(1,[4,5])$, edge checking must fail
before packaging. The opened index cannot be mentioned in
an escaping result type unless the result retains a witness
under an appropriate binder. A backend may lower the pair to
two coordinated block arguments without a heap allocation,
but it still has to preserve edge correspondence and retain
the length if the summation uses it at runtime.
